der  and perhaps i was at first but so  strong was my conviction and the belief  of dna to reduce  violent crime that i leaned into it  headfirst  no matter what the challenges that face  you in your society  and no matter how hard the fight to  overcome them i believe that all of us  has within us the power to change the  world  so if you want to change the society in  which you live or perhaps even the world  i urge you to campaign for whatever it  is that matters most  to you your community our world needs  more dna crusaders  and i share these lessons today in the  hope that maybe some of you out there  may be  motivated to connect with each other and  join forces so that we can  fight crime together just as dna is the  blueprint of life  so civil society you are the key to the  blueprint for change  thank you  hello everybody uh thanks for this  digital invitation my name is klaus  vloot  i'm a forensic investigator working at  the national crime squad of the  netherlands  part of the netherlands please today i'd  like to give you a short update  why we use the rapid id in the in the  rapid hit in the netherlands  rapid dna i should  bring this uh presentation together with  my colleague stephanie frazula  but she's very busy now with the project  with a project  a rapid id so is not unable to join this  meeting  for now i will explain why we use  the rapid rapid dna this uh  was not an easy way to start with it  because  we had to took several steps to reach  the  the goal and finally could use it in the  field  uh but i think these steps were worth  all  being because i'm i'm a forensic officer  for a long time  and i am sure rapid dna will help us  in in cases and will be a powerful tool  in  to tackle crime for now  i'd like to tell you a little bit about  the forensics in the netherlands  we have one national police force  forensics are divided in the region  so every region has a forensic  department  and they will do an investigation from a  burglary  ra