s  to other criminal contacts  so another strategy then  arrest them immediately so  the idea with real-time identification  was to combine the human observation  with the scientific observation  and we had two uh five possibilities  the fingerprints dna digital aura voice  recognition  and face recognition and we know  fingerprints and dna  are the strongest one so we are looking  for possibilities  to do an investigation and an  identification  within  two or three hours and this was possible  and i will focus now on dna because  uh that was the most important uh  investigation for us in real-time  identification  just a look back and i think until now  still  in the netherlands we work on this way  we find samples on the crime scene  dna fingerprints other samples and then  we are working working working sometimes  hours  it could be the whole day and then we  pack the samples we certified the  samples we bring it to a van  and it will transport it to a laboratory  forensics laboratory in the region then  they will investigate it and pack it  and make a registration and do a  second investigation maybe they found  blood take a swab of blood  and then they bring it to our national  forensic institute  where they only do the dna  investigations  they will start an investigation but  this will take a long time when you do  it very quickly maybe one day  when you're lucky but normally it will  take  days weeks and even months and that's  really true  so we had to speed up this process and  and  our idea was to not only the id  we're working now at the possibility to  do an investigation at the crime scene  so  we put a rapid hit but also for  fingerprints and everything else  we put the equipment in a van and we  could do  the analyze uh now at uh  a crime scene so when you find uh  maybe stabbing find blood take a sample  put it uh in in your  rapid hit and you will see it we sent it  to a laboratory to the  to the database and they compare it  this could be done in